    "information": {
      "description": "<p><em>With Rocklin Augmentics gone, Zetatech took its place in the mass market. The Newman is the best entry-level conversion around: gentle on first-timers, weak in a fight, and popular with the rich and famous who pay others to do the fighting.</em></p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> 11,800eb (V. Expensive)<br><strong>Humanity Loss:</strong> 13 (4d6)<br><strong>Frame:</strong> Sigma (12): BODY 12<br><strong>Eyes:</strong> Cybereye ×2<br><strong>Chrome:</strong> Amplified Hearing, Self-ICE, (+1 SP) Skinweave</p><p>Every body includes the standard chassis (Cyberarm ×2, Cyberaudio Suite, Cyberleg ×2, Cyberskull, an Internal Linear Frame and a Neuroport) at no HL, plus its eyes and base chrome. Going metal needs a Biosystem (bought separately) and a Hospital.</p><p><small>Item Compendium (2070) • Full Body Conversions</small></p>",
      "alias": "",
      "history": "",
      "notes": ""
    }
  },
